Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:38:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-115: the defaultView setting -- a page can open
 with its HTML beside it, as WPF's Split view (0.115.0)

WPF (Tools > Options > XAML Designer, "Default document view") can open a
document as the design view or split (the design and the markup side by side).
Here a page always opened as the design surface alone (the HTML a Shift+F7
away). New setting ht9045Designer.defaultView = design (the default, as before)
/ split: the page's HTML opens in the column beside the designer, the focus
staying on the design; not again when it is open already.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 191, panels, real VS Code 159):
smoke (design by default: nothing opened; split: Setup.HotPlate.html opened in
the column next to the designer's).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
